_guidance\": \"Port the 2.7.1 tests to the 5.0.0 API instead of copying them. Drop the Exhibitor ensemble-provider tests (`ExhibitorEnsembleProvider`, `Exhibitors`, `ExhibitorRestClient`, `DefaultExhibitorRestClient`), because that package is absent from the 5.0.0 artifact. Replace the removed static `RetryLoop.shouldRetry` and `RetryLoop.isRetryException` calls with whatever 5.0.0 exposes, for example `RetryLoop.getDefaultRetrySleeper()` or `RetryLoop.callWithRetry`. Reach retry-policy behavior through public classes such as `RetryNTimes` and `ExponentialBackoffRetry`. Check the 5.0.0 jar for the actual public API before writing code. Keep the existing ZooKeeper dependency in `build.gradle`, bumped to a version compatible with curator-client 5.0.0 (ZooKeeper 3.6.x line) if the build does not already resolve it transitively.\",\n+      \"risks\": [\n+        \"The 5.0.0 API removal list is inferred only from the compile errors shown in the truncated log. More missing symbols may appear after the first set is fixed.\",\n+        \"Dropping the Exhibitor tests may reduce dynamic-access coverage relative to 2.7.1, if those tests exercised reflective access.\",\n+        \"curator-client 5.0.0 pulls in ZooKeeper 3.6.x, which may add transitive dependencies or require reflection metadata not present for 2.7.1.\"\n+      ],\n+      \"applied_setup\": [],\n+      \"input_evidence\": [\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"issue\",\n+          \"summary\": \"#9364 [Automation] javac compile fails for org.apache.curator:curator-client:5.0.0; label=fails-javac-compile; body_chars=8015\"\n+        },\n+        {\n+          \"name\": \"existing_tests\",\n+          \"summary\": \"7 existing test file path(s) included\"\n+        }\n+      ],\n+      \"current_library\": \"org.apache.curator:curator-client:2.7.1\",\n+      \"new_version\": \"5.0.0\",\n+      \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n+      \"input_tokens_used\": 2,\n+      \"output_tokens_used\": 1140\n+    },\n+    \"metrics\": {